From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: run a frame-capped game at the lowest refresh
 rate the cap divides

Steam's frame rate slider sets a target frame rate, and gamescope picks
the panel refresh rate for it: the highest valid rate the target
divides ("refresh doubling"), which only lowers latency. On the AYN
Odin 2 Portal (60 and 120 Hz) every usual cap, 30 or 60 fps, therefore
ran the panel at 120 Hz, refreshing the panel and the DSI link twice as
often as the game draws.

Pick the lowest such rate instead, for battery life on a handheld: a 30
or 60 fps cap now runs at 60 Hz; 40 fps, 120 fps and uncapped stay at
120 Hz.
---
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -1146,8 +1146,9 @@
 	{
 		auto rates = GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetValidDynamicRefreshRates();
 
-		// Find highest mode to do refresh doubling with.
-		for ( auto rate = rates.rbegin(); rate != rates.rend(); rate++ )
+		// Find the lowest mode the frame rate divides: a panel refreshing no faster than
+		// the game draws uses the least power (doubling would only lower latency).
+		for ( auto rate = rates.begin(); rate != rates.end(); rate++ )
 		{
 			if (*rate % target_fps == 0)
 			{
